The changes are introduced in order to parse new relayer fee format. The endpoint `/fee` will return the following json:

```
 {
  fee: {
    deposit: string;
    transfer: string;
    withdrawal: string;
    permittableDeposit: string;
  };
  oneByteFee: string;
  nativeConvertFee: string;
}
```

So the library should distinguish the base fee component for the different transaction types

Library still supports all previous fee formats

Due to introducing `nativeConvertFee` field a few function signatures have been changed:
- `atomicTxFee(txType: TxType, withdrawSwap: bigint = 0n)`: added optional `withdrawSwap` parameter
- `feeEstimate(transfersGwei: bigint[], txType: TxType, withdrawSwap: bigint = 0n, updateState: boolean = true)`: added optional `withdrawSwap` parameter
- `calcMaxAvailableTransfer(txType: TxType, relayerFee?: RelayerFee, withdrawSwap: bigint = 0n, updateState: boolean = true)`: added optional `withdrawSwap` and `relayerFee` parameters
- `getTransactionParts(txType: TxType, transfers: TransferRequest[],  relayerFee?: RelayerFee, withdrawSwap: bigint = 0n, updateState: boolean = true, allowPartial: boolean = false)`: added optional `withdrawSwap` and `relayerFee` parameters
